{#
  The group filter chips.

  Labels come from content/settings/team-groups.yaml — the same file that
  supplies the section headings — so a renamed group updates both at once.

  "Everyone" / "Wszyscy" is defined separately (`all_filter`) because it is not
  a group: it has no heading and no members, only a label and the reserved
  `all` key that team-filter.js checks for.

  SEMANTICS (corrected in Phase 5 — see docs/TEAM_ACCESSIBILITY_REMEDIATION.md)
  These controls filter a roster; they do not switch tab panels. So this is a
  labelled GROUP of native buttons, not a tablist:

    role="group" + aria-label ... names the set of controls
    aria-pressed ............... carries the on/off state of each toggle

  It is deliberately NOT a formal ARIA tab widget: `role="tab"` would promise
  arrow-key navigation and owned tabpanels that do not exist here.

  The classes are unchanged (`filter-bar`, `chip`, `active`) because all styling
  keys off them — the correction is invisible.
#}
    <div class="filter-bar reveal" role="group" aria-label="{{ t.team.filterBarLabel }}">
      <button class="chip active" data-filter="{{ teamGroups.all_filter.key }}" aria-pressed="true">{{ teamGroups.all_filter[locale.code].filter_label }}</button>
{%- for group in teamGroups.groups %}
      <button class="chip" data-filter="{{ group.key }}" aria-pressed="false">{{ group[locale.code].filter_label }}</button>
{%- endfor %}
    </div>
